2. English translation
   File: tool/src/main/assets/en-pickthall.txt
   Marmaduke Pickthall, "The Meaning of the Glorious Koran"
   (Alfred A. Knopf, New York, 1930).
   Public domain: Pickthall died in 1936, so the work is in the public domain
   in countries with a term of life plus 70 years or less; in the United
   States, works published in 1930 entered the public domain on 1 January
   2026. The digital text is Tanzil's edition (translation id en.pickthall),
   distributed exactly as Tanzil publishes it. Compared with the 1930 print,
   Tanzil's edition has light editorial normalization: transliterations
   without accents ("Lam. Mim." for "Lâm. Mîm."), some capitalization, and
   in some verses "deity" where the print has "God" (e.g. 2:255). The same
   edition is used by Quran.com and alquran.cloud. These editorial changes
   are minor and not themselves copyrightable; the translation remains in
   the public domain.

